+Implement Feature SC-08 (Contractual Scope Boundary & Creep Detector):
+
+1. In `src/utils/scopeGovernance.ts`:
+   Export function `detectScopeCreep(params: {
+     contractBoqItemIds: string[];
+     approvedVariationIds: string[];
+     siteTasks: Array<{
+       taskId: string;
+       description: string;
+       boqItemId?: string;
+       variationId?: string;
+       qty: number;
+       estimatedRate: number;
+     }>;
+   })`:
+   - Identify unmapped tasks: any siteTask where:
+     `(!task.boqItemId || !contractBoqItemIds.includes(task.boqItemId)) && (!task.variationId || !approvedVariationIds.includes(task.variationId))`
+   - Calculate `creepCostEstimate` as the sum of `(task.qty * task.estimatedRate)` for all unmapped tasks.
+   - Return `{ hasScopeCreep: unmappedTasks.length > 0, unmappedTasksCount: unmappedTasks.length, creepCostEstimate, unmappedTasks }`.
+
+2. In `tests/scope-governance.test.mjs`:
+   Write unit tests using `node:test` and `node:assert`:
+   - Test 1: Clean project with all tasks mapped to valid BOQ or approved variation (hasScopeCreep = false, creepCostEstimate = 0).
+   - Test 2: Project with unmapped site tasks flagged properly (hasScopeCreep = true, creepCostEstimate accurately calculated).
+   - Test 3: Variation-backed tasks accepted (tasks with approvedVariationId are not flagged as creep).
+
+Do not create any UI components. Pure backend logic and test suite only.

